/substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!miyz!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F206f33a1-c6bf-4019-b29b-ed5cb34672a5_1038x449.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!miyz!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F206f33a1-c6bf-4019-b29b-ed5cb34672a5_1038x449.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><ul><li><p>Mid-terms may actually be bullish due to future gridlock.</p><ul><li><p>The “not-normal” economic policies, such as drastic sweeping tariff scares, may be coming to an end as the House and Senate will be in gridlock. This will create more predictable scenarios for institutional investors, which they love predictable markets. </p></li></ul></li><li><p>Pokemon, a risk-off asset, continues to show strength (shown in video)</p></li></ul><p>Considering all of this, despite the volatility last week, we can clearly see there is no real reason to be panicked. Scary Friday…but nothing broke. Again, trend remains up. </p><p>Last week we shifted up the portfolio some, eliminating some of the weaker positions or selling some off for profit. </p><h4><strong>You can <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/here-is-my-plan-in-this-crazy-stock\">see the portfolio changes by clicking here.</a></strong></h4><p>My focus remains on recession resistant assets. Last week was a perfect example of why I am NOT interested in tech. Unless you are a short term trader, these stocks have been harsh holds both mid-term and long-term. </p><p>I will also add, that the <strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/stocktok-etf-20?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok ETF 2.0 (click here)</a></strong> did not get the memo about a bear market. In fact, it is breaking out to the upside today. The original StockTok ETF is up nearly 22% to the S&amp;P 500’S 9.5%, while version 2 just surged past with strength. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wI09!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Ff1c684c5-9c4e-48ce-a6c9-38089afbb1e0_864x461.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!wI09!,w_424,c_